  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1226 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nAs of 12:30 AM CST, temperatures across the area are in the upper \n40s to low 50s with winds out of the north at 15 to 20 mph, gusting \nbetween 25 and 35 mph with some locally higher wind gusts noted\naround Pierre. These gusts are expected to last through the \nday. Portions of central SD may see some wind gusts as high as \n45 mph through the morning. A Wind Advisory remains in effect \nfor this area through 11 AM MST. Rain showers will also continue\nthrough most of the day today and through most of Wednesday for\nnortheast SD and west central MN. Accumulations across \nnortheast SD have ranged between 1 and 3 inches already, highest\nacross east central SD, particularly around the Watertown area.\nThe chance of an additional inch of accumulation or more \nthrough Wednesday is around 50 to 70% mainly east of the James \nRiver and highest along I-29.\n\nTemperatures through the period will be closer to average than the \nlast week or so with highs in the 40s east of the Missouri River and \nin the low 50s west. Models are starting to show a warm up back into \nthe mid to upper 50s across the entire area for next weekend into \nthe beginning of next work week. Winds Wednesday afternoon behind \nthe low are expected to gust between 30 and 35 mph across the \nmajority of the forecast area. These gusts will die off during the \nevening and into the overnight except for on the eastern slope of \nthe Prairie Coteau of northeast SD.",
